ion generations, and explicit Configuration 4.0.0 migration. Preserve accepted historical Config 1/2/3 and peer identity/SSH work; consume it through reviewed integration. This is pending runtime work, not delivered by catalogue adoption.\n\n### Scope\n\nrelux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0 commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6; sections 6.6, 11.10.2, 11.10.3. Own credential custody and trust-generation APIs, durable preview/apply/rollback and credential exclusion; RPC transport/admission stays TASK-260830-z1yxg9, conformance TASK-260830-2x16gz.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nExact closed Config-4 and Host Trust Store readers; explicit out-of-band enrollment, unique credential-to-host mapping, fresh-key bounded rotation and immediate revocation; current-generation mutation authorization; owner-only atomic crash-durable writes; exact-preview confirmed Config-4 migration with complete peer enrollment; refuse partial/unreadable/missing state, downgrade and implicit legacy fallback. Positive and narrowing-negative production tests, platform custody and crash evidence; no secret replication. Resume only after signed STORY-260908-18woqo lands.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4190`\n- Content digest: `sha256:d3bef7ae84af0f92b4c4a7ac2563d018075992f43e5d1e7e13238dbc3f26e9ab`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2958`\n- Content digest: `sha256:74609054ec9524be4f3f932e107edf394a100181c674252115117b17851c0cce`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_resume-after-pr207.md\nResume preserved credentials/config implementation after root confirms PR207 is landed and the canonical Curator CLI is installed. This is a recovery of completed work, not a fresh implementation. Read results.md, retry2.md, retry3.md and the retained validation failures. Prior run de0df2 was deliberately cancelled to stop deterministic repeated gate21 failures, not because its candidate was discarded.\nVerify actual canonical CLI provenance and refresh-candidate help before using it. Preserve the RPC backup manifest (15 files) and parked delta; do not absorb RPC into this leaf. Preserve checkpointed SSH/peer work and all hosttrust/Config4 changes. The shared Story base must move from c1eff01 to current protected AX trunk containing the v0.6.0 adoption. Combine current trunk coherently with the candidate, resolve real conflicts preserving both intended changes, and use the repaired explicit managed refresh-candidate from the live producer with its exclusive lease. Do not selectively vendor catalogue files merely to make gate21 pass, weaken validation, edit board registries, or manually synthesize checkpoint commits.\nRefresh preserves candidate bytes rather than merging incoming source for you; verify the resulting complete candidate incorporates the adopted catalogue/specpin/ownership/config contracts. If replay conflicts require a supported resolution packet, bind exact checkpoint/path/content digests. Any further reusable tool defect goes to root with evidence; no unchanged doomed handoff or retry storm.\nRun applicable local validation on the refreshed candidate, with exact-head/source provenance. Reconcile new source and negative evidence from retry3. Full scope and accepted RPC caller boundary remain; no invented guarantees for dispatch after shared-lock release or Windows DACL validation. Publish the normal next CR through handoff only once prerequisites are satisfied. Do not integrate or push main. Independent review will follow.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-current-base.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-current-base.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2815`\n- Content digest: `sha256:70f5f797cfdf81e5a2b274846e317223c2cbbbdf1c4b41b59fe46d09dc70acd8`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev3.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev3.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3001`\n- Content digest: `sha256:553782db41a386bdf1c444d40fbca3ff396aa0a0913e59e6ea0d46d7f7bc7ada`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2426`\n- Content digest: `sha256:bd0585b3521067e2cbe22909ee6deb2ae86e7b8ff727b0be583fce953f896a6b`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3-current.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3-current.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3388`\n- Content digest: `sha256:bac7ff39d3935a3998425dd06b28bf6c765aae293118d2e00e36da053a9e7765`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev4.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev4.md`\n\n- Byte count: `5824`\n- Content digest: `sha256:53167f936d6b2ed658b2802cd25dd132247b26e9bb7db9e6b9d567d7cb0710ff`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr5.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr5.md`\n\n- Byte count: `5242`\n- Content digest: `sha256:475525ab791e46b69f70673f574be35fa008dec5e419593244f4e0fcf0c62b4b`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev5.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2