{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c49f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ac04-3aa6-7f83-a640-4d27d55c8cba"},"sequence":170,"recorded_at":1780531400000335,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"792618d5-7c92-47f4-9c2f-44170e04457d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"792618d5-7c92-47f4-9c2f-44170e04457d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"792618d5-7c92-47f4-9c2f-44170e04457d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ac04-be06-74a1-b33b-7fc1136f7cf7"},"task_id":"01a0ac04-be06-74a1-b33b-7fc1136f7cf7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ac04-be06-74a1-b33b-7fc1136f7cf7","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev7.md`.\n1|Rework the credentials/Config4 candidate of TASK-260909-2ez769 after the CR7 independent changes-requested verdict by RUN-260916-17a623 (Astra low). Read TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev7.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_review-logbook-rev7.md and materialize TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev7.zip (census-plants/ with five plant files and probe-census.py, TestReviewerForeignHoldCannotWriteLockedPair, TestReviewerFailedReplaceRestoreSerializesReader, logs). Base is still the managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903; CR7 candidate tree fca43ac48ee7fea12e7a8429322b2d9ce1a58cf8 in .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree — continue from it. Preserve the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves, the parked RPC artifacts and the control-root backup with their recorded hashes; no RPC transport; no manual commits; no direct .task-board edits; no self-acceptance. Superseded briefs are scope context only; this brief governs.\n2|\n3|Good news first: the reviewer confirmed the CR6 F1/F2 product repairs (legacy migrate under WithExclusiveHold, resolveFailedReplace keeping intent, serialized restore against a surviving reader) and the seven original probes plus the six compensation races — do not touch those mechanisms. Both remaining findings are P2 defects of the prevention instrument, and the task cannot be accepted while the instrument's completeness claim is false.\n4|\n5|F2 (capability not bound to its resource): hosttrust.HeldExclusive stores only an atomic released bit, so a live token obtained from an unrelated store authorizes writeTempReplace on another store's config (TestReviewerForeignHoldCannotWriteLockedPair, -race, exit 1). Bind the capability to the coordination resource: the token must carry the identity of the lock/store it was minted by (store root or lock file identity, plus the pairing of config and trust under that store), and every protected mutation helper (hosttrust and config requireHold) must verify that the target path or store belongs to that identity, rejecting a live token from a different store with a typed refusal; keep zero-token and released-token refusals and same-store handles usable per the actual lock model. Port the reviewer probe RED first, keep it committed, and add a narrowing plant that admits a wrong-resource token while retaining zero/released refusals.\n6|\n7|F1 (static census gate incompleteness, second recurrence): the gate resolves the spelling \"os\" rather than the imported package identity, recognizes function-value escapes only as bare identifiers, and walks package initializers only when the initializer is itself a FuncLit; the reviewer's five plants (direct os.WriteFile control; os.WriteFile stored in a package map and called through lookup; `import fs \"os\"`; package initializer invoking a factory that returns an os.WriteFile closure; backend method value osMigrationFileSystem{}.Rename stored and called indirectly) were detected 1 of 5. Do not extend the syntactic scanner with more names. Rebuild the gate on the type checker: load the hosttrust and config packages with go/types (golang.org/x/tools/go/packages or go/importer with type info), identify filesystem-mutating operations by resolved package path and object identity (os.Rename/Remove/RemoveAll/Create/CreateTemp/OpenFile/WriteFile/MkdirTemp/Link/Symlink/Truncate and the backend interface methods) regardless of import alias or spelling, treat every method value, method expression, function value, closure, map/struct-stored function and interface-satisfying implementation that reaches such an operation as a writer, walk every initializer and immediately invoked function, and fail closed on any call whose callee cannot be resolved. The allowlist is the set of censused definitions (exact package path + receiver + method), nothing else. Commit the five reviewer plants, the original six controls and at least two new shapes of your own (an interface method satisfied by a rogue type invoked through the interface; a generic helper parameterized over the writer) as executable controls that must fail the gate, keep TestReviewerRoguePlantExecutes-style witnesses that prove each plant really mutates bytes, and keep the preserve-token behavioral mutant. Update the census document so its completeness statement is exactly what the type-checked gate enforces, with the exempt-by-proof rows stated as enforced properties, not prose.\n8|\n9|Retain rows 15 and 21 as accounted; update the 21-row AC matrix; rerun the hosttrust and config mutation batteries on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, a neutral SURVIVED control through the same harness and exits from subprocess return codes; no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills. Full configured local validation before the normal producer handoff; no hosted CI. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first. Budget: hand off no later than 3 hours in (the runtime's 26-command suite runs after your handoff). Leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev8.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev8.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev8.tar.gz, then hand off through task-board and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.","final_result":true}}}
