usiveHold constructs, verified live and expired on unlock, with a zero-token runtime refusal (ErrExclusiveHoldRequired); a fail-closed static gate that scans any receiver, package-level initializers and nested literals, resolves local aliases, flags helper escapes as values and every direct os.* filesystem call outside the exact backend definitions, with six executable controls (the four CR6 reviewer shapes verbatim plus two producer shapes). Verify the instrument first: can a writer obtain or forge a HeldExclusive outside the lock (zero value, copied token after unlock, a token from another store instance, reflection/unsafe aside)? does the static gate really fail on a new shape you invent (for example a function value stored in a map or struct field and called indirectly, a closure returned from a helper, an interface method satisfied by a rogue type, a `var` initializer in a new file, or a call through a package alias import)? are the \"exempt-by-proof\" rows (credential files, lock creation, staging writeTempFile, ACL install secureStaged) actually unable to touch the committed pair, and is the proof more than prose?\n4|\n5|Then verify the two CR6 P1 rows: F1 legacy migrate now opens the coordinating store (openLegacyStore) and runs source revalidation and the durable replacement under WithExclusiveHold, refusing ErrMigrationStaleSource when the source moved including after a completed Config4 commit — rerun TestReviewerLegacyCannotOverwriteCommittedV4 on the exact candidate (the producer says it now blocks on the held lock; confirm the final state can no longer be the overwrite and that TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4 asserts the final state), and check the documented side effect that opening creates the owner-only store skeleton when absent; F2 JointCommit routes every replace error through resolveFailedReplace under the same hold — only configuration still equal to the source pin aborts with the marker removed; durable replacement, diverged bytes or unreadable state run the compensation protocol and otherwise keep the marker — rerun TestReviewerFailedReplacementCannotLoseIntent and TestReviewerFailedRollbackCannotLoseIntent, check apply and rollback, surviving readers and reopen (TestApplyV4/RollbackV4FailedReplaceKeepsIntent, ...KeepsMarkerWhenRestoreFails, TestResolveFailedReplaceKeepsMarker), and probe one interleaving the producer did not: a replace error after a successful rename where the restore succeeds but a surviving reader converged in between. Keep the CR5 compensation races, the seven original probes and the CR4 repairs green.\n6|\n7|Retain rows 15 and 21 exactly as CR5/CR6 accounted them; re-derive the 21-row AC table from source and named tests; check the hosttrust and config batteries (per-plant raw logs, neutral SURVIVED control through the same harness, exits from subprocess return codes, the new token-gate and F1/F2 plants) with no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills; confirm RPC backup 15/15 and parked 11/11 hashes with zero overlap against the 61 candidate paths; confirm checkpointed SSH/peer predecessors are preserved and no RPC transport was implemented.\n8|\n9|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; free disk is tight (about 11 GB) — keep scratch small, delete only your own scratch, and run `go clean -cache` if you must. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev7.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev7.zip, complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260909-2ez769, revision=7, evidence=TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev7.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2 classes and repeat-of named. Model: codex gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
