ity/traceability.go, task-board.config.json, untracked UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md and internal/rpcwire/. Root inspected tracked changes: RPC staged docs/ownership hash and one RPC fuzz gate. These are not credentials work.\n7|\n8|A verified byte-for-byte backup exists at the CONTROL ROOT /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910 with manifest.json (15 files, SHA256, original head, tracked/untracked classification), tracked.patch and files/. Re-verify every source/backup byte and current status before changing any listed path. If new or different foreign changes exist, preserve them in an additional verified snapshot first. Attach a task-scoped preservation archive/outcome to the RPC task and record restoration instructions before separation. Preserve original file modes and all evidence; no secrets should be printed.\n9|\n10|To free the candidate scope, you may park ONLY this enumerated RPC delta: after durable verified backup, restore each of the four individually named tracked paths to its checkpoint blob and move the enumerated untracked RPC files into task-scoped preservation storage outside the worktree. Verify every moved byte remains recoverable and retain the backup. No repo-wide reset/restore/checkout/clean, no deletion of original work without verified preservation, no absorption of the RPC delta into this CR. Do not remove other files or .temp evidence. The RPC task remains pending and its old v0.5.0 unresolved note is historical; current v0.6.0 credential requirements settle the direction.\n11|\n12|Then use the documented managed workspace/base refresh flow to incorporate current main and v0.6.0 while preserving checkpointed signed commits and board authority. Do not hand-edit .task-board or hand-synthesize commits, do not reset an accepted checkpoint or change its identity behind the manager. If tooling refuses a safe base transition, report the exact refusal and handle promptly to root so the reusable tool can be fixed; do not spend the run inventing local bypasses.\n13|\n14|## Delivery\n15|Read the Curator-managed Go testing skill. Implement production-entry tests, meaningful narrowing negatives, actual platform custody and crash-durability evidence. Include an applied compiling harmless SURVIVED control and a named-test KILLED control for mutation instrumentation; preserve mutant source/digest, standalone exits, logs and truthful final counts. Reuse stable evidence where appropriate, avoid repeated broad suites without a changed candidate or failure. Required repository/runtime gates remain in force; CI runs only locally, never enable hosted Actions.\n16|\n17|Use /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. One writer for this Story. No changes to the active sessquery Story. Keep task checklist/notes/outcomes current, deliver complete task scope, perform producer handoff and exit promptly so runtime publishes the CR. Separate reviewer will be Codex gpt-6-astra medium. Do not accept your own CR or land. All managed commits must retain Ivan Oparin SSH signatures.","final_result":true}}}
