etected**. Every plant is a new non-test source\n23|file in the immutable candidate copy. Each invocation runs both\n24|TestWritePathCensusGate and TestReviewerRoguePlantExecutes with -count=1.\n25|The witness calls the planted production-position function, replacing real file\n26|bytes without acquiring an authorization hold. Every witness PASSED.\n27|\n28|| Plant | Census | Process exit |\n29||---|---|---:|\n30|| Direct os.WriteFile (positive detection control) | rejected | 1 |\n31|| os.WriteFile stored in a package map and called through map lookup | MISSED | 0 |\n32|| `import fs \"os\"`; fs.WriteFile | MISSED | 0 |\n33|| Package initializer invokes factory returning closure using os.WriteFile | MISSED | 0 |\n34|| osMigrationFileSystem{}.Rename stored as a method value, called indirectly | MISSED | 0 |\n35|\n36|Sources and raw logs are in census-plants/; probe-census.py reproduces the five\n37|runs. The direct-control exit 1 is a real census assertion failure, not a build\n38|failure; the four green executions prove the escapes. In particular the backend\n39|method-value plant bypasses the token by invoking the ordinary production backend.\n40|\n41|Required rework: enforce the claimed domain using package/symbol-aware mutation\n42|and function-value handling, or explicit fail-closed restrictions for unresolved\n43|flows. Walk all executable initializer descendants. Apply the rule to backend\n44|method references as well as calls; do not treat unreadable/unresolved forms as\n45|safe. Keep these executable controls, the original six controls and the\n46|preserve-token behavioral mutant. A list of these specific new names is not a\n47|class-level repair. Until then the census's statement that out-of-protocol\n48|writers cannot exist is false, and its exemptions are not a completeness proof.\n49|\n50|## F2 — P2: a live capability from a different store authorizes the target writer\n51|\n52|Repeat-of: CR6 F3's prevention instrument; newly introduced capability weakness.\n53|`internal/hosttrust/hold.go:26-33` stores only an atomic released bit. Neither\n54|hosttrust.requireHold nor config.requireHold (`migration.go:303`) relates that\n55|bit to a lock, store root or mutation target. The hold proves that SOME lock is\n56|held, not the authorization lock protecting the pair being replaced.\n57|\n58|TestReviewerForeignHoldCannotWriteLockedPair, run with -race, fails (exit 1):\n59|\n60|1. Open a target fixture and an unrelated store at a distinct state root.\n61|2. A separate goroutine holds the target store's exclusive authorization lock,\n62|   waiting on a channel. It never lends its hold to the writer.\n63|3. A planted production-position reviewerForeignWrite obtains the unrelated\n64|   store's genuine token through WithExclusiveHold and passes it to the existing\n65|   writeTempReplace for the target config.\n66|4. The replacement succeeds while the target holder is still blocked; a disk\n67|   read verifies the replacement bytes. TestWritePathCensusGate PASSES on this\n68|   same plant because it is syntactically inside WithExclusiveHold.\n69|\n70|See foreign-hold-production-final.log and probes/config/. No zero token,\n71|reflection, unsafe or unlock race is involved. The corresponding same-store\n72|serialization, zero-token and released-token tests pass; they do not cover this\n73|wrong-resource case. Both advertised enforcement layers admit the new writer.\n74|\n75|Required rework: bind the capability and each protected mutation to the same\n76|coordination resource, including the config/trust pairing, and reject a live\n77|capability from an unrelated store. Add this production-position negative and a\n78|narrowing plant that admits a wrong-resource token while retaining zero/released\n79|refusals. Keep same-resource handles usable according to the actual lock model.\n80|The current shipped callers were not found to select a foreign token; severity\n81|is P2 for the broken mandatory guard/instrument, not a newly demonstrated P1\n82|in the existing ApplyV4/RollbackV4 call chain.\n83|\n84|## CR6 F1 and F2 are repaired in the exercised production paths\n85|\n86|- Legacy migrate now opens the coordinating store and performs source\n87|  revalidation plus replacement under WithExclusiveHold. The exact original\n88|  synchronous TestReviewerLegacyCannotOverwriteCommittedV4 now times out at\n89|  5 seconds (exit 1), blocked in exclusiveHold. This is serialization evidence,\n90|  NOT a passing test. TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4 passes and\n91|  checks final Config4/generation+1 after refusing the delayed legacy source.\n92|  Source inspection confirms both version and exact-byte revalidation. Opening\n93|  an absent store creates its owner-only skeleton, as documented; it does not\n94|  silently create trust.json.\n95|- Both exact TestReviewerFailedReplacementCannotLoseIntent and\n96|  TestReviewerFailedRollbackCannotLoseIntent pass. Failed replace now enters\n97|  resolveFailedReplace under the continuous hold. Source-equal state aborts;\n98|  durable replacement restores under compensation or retains the marker.\n99|  The committed marker-kept/reopen tests pass in the package suite.\n100|- The new TestReviewerFailedReplaceRestoreSerializesReader exercises apply AND\n101|  rollback: replacement rename succeeds, its sync fails, the first restore fails,\n102|  and the compensation restore pauses before succeeding. A surviving coherent\n103|  reader attempts convergence during that pause and remains blocked; after\n104|  release it sees the exact source bytes and unchanged generation. Reopen sees\n105|  the same clean abort and no marker. Both subtests pass with -race. A reader\n106|  cannot converge 'in between' through this actual locked path.\n107|- All seven original probes and all six CR5 compensation races pass with -race.\n108|  Child crash probes retain real process termination and cross-process locking.\n109|\n110|The exempt credential path uses fresh digest directories, fixed filenames and\n111|use-time custody checks; lock creation uses O_EXCL and never replaces a live\n112|inode; config writeTempFile stages through CreateTemp without publishing;\n113|secureStaged is ACL setup at the inspected call sites. These current callers\n114|are consistent with the stated exemptions. Their prose does not establish that\n115|new callers cannot reach committed state: F1/F2 defeat that prevention claim.\n116|No native Windows runtime, physical power-loss, post-lock-release dispatch or\n117|secret-exclusion consumer guarantee is added here.\n118|\n119|## AC accounting\n120|\n121|**19 of 21 functional AC rows driven**, with the existing flow tests passing\n122|within the bounds below. The 21 rows were checked against pinned sections 6.6,\n123|11.10.2 and 11.10.3 and their named candidate tests. This is the established\n124|functional decomposition, not exhaustive normative-clause or all-gates mutation\n125|coverage. The newly claimed class-level writer instrument fails F1/F2, so these\n126|passing rows do not justify acceptance. Rows 15 and 21 retain CR5/CR6 bounds.\n127|\n128|| # | Row | Production call / named test | Result |\n129||---|---|---|---|\n130|| 1 | Closed Config4 | config.Decode / TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals | pass |\n131|| 2 | Historical compat + explicit migration | config.Migrate/migrate / TestMigrateRefusesV4Target, TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade, TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4, TestLegacyMigrateConvergesUnreplacedMarkerThenCommits, TestLegacyMigrateRefusesAfterReplacementLanded | pass (was CR6 FAIL) |\n132|| 3 | Closed trust document | hosttrust.DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals | pass |\n133|| 4 | Missing/corrupt/unreadable trust | hosttrust ReadSnapshot / TestReadSnapshotMissingStore, TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty, TestReadSnapshotRefusesUnreadableMarker | pass |\n134|| 5 | Fresh issuance | hosttrust IssueCredential / TestIssueCredentialProfile | pass |\n135|| 6 | Exact profile + time bounds | hosttrust VerifyProfile / TestVerifyProfileRefusals, TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry | pass |\n136|| 7 | Explicit tuple enrollment | hosttrust Store.Enroll / TestEnrollRefusals | pass; OOB human verification remains operator act |\n137|| 8 | Mapping uniqueness | hosttrust DecodeTrust+admitEntry / duplicate-root/key/digest rows | pass |\n138|| 9 | Rotation/retirement bounds | hosttrust Rotate, MarkRetiring / TestRotateBoundedWindow, TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry | pass |\n139|| 10 | Revocation tombstones | hosttrust Revoke, Enroll / TestRevokeTombstone, TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls | pass |\n140|| 11 | Old-generation mutation refusal | hosttrust WithMutationAuthorization / TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration, TestMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleAfterConvergence | pass |\n141|| 12 | Shared authorization serialization | hosttrust Open/openLock, WithMutationAuthorization+Revoke / TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock, TestConcurrentOpenAttachesToExistingLock, TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation, TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithSeparateStoreRevocation | pass |\n142|| 13 | Coherent config+trust snapshot | config LoadCoherent / surviving-reader crash tests, six compensation races, F1/F2 ports, marker-kept reopen tests | pass (was CR6 FAIL) |\n143|| 14 | Unix owner custody | hosttrust Open, ValidateCustody / TestCustodyRefusals, TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory | pass on darwin |\n144|| 15 | Windows equivalent ACLs | hosttrust verifyOwner/installOwnerOnlyACL/secureStaged / custody_windows_test.go (7 native tests) | NOT DRIVEN: code + tests present, runtime unverified (no runner) |\n145|| 16 | Complete peers + selected credential | config PreviewV4 / TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment, TestPreviewV4CredentialGates | pass |\n146|| 17 | Exact preview + confirmation | config ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch, TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops | pass |\n147|| 18 | Current source/generation apply | config applyV4+JointCommit / TestApplyV4StaleSource, TestApplyV4StaleGeneration, revalidate* tests | pass, incl. in-lock revalidation |\n148|| 19 | Crash-durable config/trust pair | config applyV4/rollbackV4 + hosttrust JointCommit/resolveFailedReplace/compensateLocked/Recover/converge / TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration (fixed), surviving-reader crash tests, barrier matrix, 6 compensation race tests, F2 ports + marker-kept tests | pass (was CR6 FAIL) |\n149|| 20 | Explicit backup rollback | config RollbackV4 / TestRollbackV4*, TestPublishedBackupNamesStayExcluded, TestApplyV4BackupIsClassifiedConfigCopy, TestRollbackV4FailedReplaceKeepsIntent, TestRollbackV4FailedReplaceKeepsMarkerWhenRestoreFails | pass (was CR6 FAIL) |\n150|| 21 | Secret exclusion across export surfaces | hosttrust MatchExcludedFromReplication/ExcludedConfigDirName / matcher tests + persisted handoff + owner notes; diagnostics unowned | NOT DRIVEN: matcher enforced, no consumer calls it yet |\n151|\n152|\n153|Row 15: NOT DRIVEN. Windows equivalent ACL code and seven native tests exist;\n154|cross-build/vet is not runtime DACL evidence. Windows backup ACL inheritance\n155|remains a bound. Row 21: NOT DRIVEN. Matcher-only evidence and persisted consumer\n156|handoff; no consumer enforcement call yet, diagnostics still unowned. RPC\n157|TLS/hello/dispatch/watchdog/stream integration stays with the RPC owner. No\n158|mesh-wide revocation or externally authenticated operator action is inferred.\n159|\n160|## Validation, provenance and limitations\n161|\n162|- Independently ran extracted-candidate config/hosttrust/peeridentity tests\n163|  -count=1 -cover: exit 0; 93.5% / 78.0% / 97.5%, Go 1.25.5 darwin/arm64.\n164|  Independently ran the nine prior probes (seven original plus two CR6 partial\n165|  replacements), six compensation races, legacy async port and new two-case\n166|  compensation-reader interleaving with -race: exit 0. Census/foreign-hold\n167|  attacks and legacy synchronous timeout have the real exits recorded above.\n168|- Verified all 61 changed candidate paths byte-for-byte against the immutable\n169|  tree; all also match live worktree bytes. Base signature verifies (exit 0).\n170|  RPC backup 15/15 and parked 11/11 hashes match; zero overlap with the 61 paths.\n171|  SSH transport unchanged; peeridentity delta only v4_interop_test.go. The patch\n172|  digest is 234f5ad8c5473c35ed500259a23de37373df12fe57375730b2fea556cf6dde0f.\n173|  Normative SPEC.v0.6.0.md matches the pin for\n174|  0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6.\n175|- Audited, not reran, both producer mutation batteries. All 34 hosttrust and\n176|  39 config source hashes match the candidate. All 43 plants match exactly once\n177|  and archived mutant source equals the expected overlay. Raw logs contain the\n178|  expected named failures, nonempty execution and no compilation-failure kills.\n179|  Hosttrust: 32 narrowing + 1 separately classified call-site kill, neutral exit\n180|  0. Config: 9 semantic + 1 separately classified label-precision kill, neutral\n181|  exit 0. Both neutrals use the same harness. The token-preserving compensation\n182|  reorder is killed by behavior, not merely the source checker. These batteries\n183|  do not cover the new F1/F2 counterexamples.\n184|- The handoff validation artifact reports 26/26 command shards green, but is\n185|  explicitly truncated (5,128,824 bytes omitted). Its visible build/vet commands\n186|  exit 0; the aggregate is not a raw complete replay of every required job.\n187|  The omitted commands' full outputs were not independently verified, and this\n188|  reviewer did not rerun the full repository/fuzz/build matrix. The producer\n189|  outcome claims those passed. Do not convert those claims or truncated logs\n190|  into complete local-check certification. Handoff board validation reports\n191|  366 issues with exit 0 (producer outcome said 201); neither proves clean board.\n192|- The first attempt to set up the production foreign-token plant used the wrong\n193|  scratch-relative path. Its log is marked invalid-setup and is not evidence\n194|  for that plant. The earlier direct-helper foreign-token experiment held both\n195|  locks in one goroutine and is superseded. The decisive final probe places the\n196|  target holder in a separate goroutine, installs the new production-position\n197|  writer and runs the gate and behavioral test together under -race.\n198|- Canonical CLI provenance and readiness recorded; the PATH wrapper execs\n199|  /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Required project-management,\n200|  architecture-diagrams and Curator go-testing-tools instructions read. No\n201|  diagram or installation needed. Missing worktree-local skill paths were\n202|  resolved to the main checkout's Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill.\n203|  Directive reads succeeded with no directives.\n204|\n205|## Verdict and route\n206|\n207|**Changes requested → to-dev. Do not accept CR7.** Two P2 defects in the mandatory\n208|class-level enforcement instrument remain. No new P1 is asserted in the existing\n209|migration paths. Repair the instrument with the executable controls above,\n210|preserve the passing F1/F2 repairs and all foreign RPC/SSH/peer bytes, then publish\n211|a new managed candidate. Ordinary implementable rework; no external blocker or\n212|human decision. Review evidence and logbook are attached before routing.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
